      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should focus the narrative on the comparative gains and the \"preventative\" success, such as preventing potential coral die-offs during a peak bleaching event, rather than relying solely on the raw growth percentage. Highlight the 5% as a significant metric when viewed against baseline conditions from years prior or compared to the decline seen in neighboring regions without intervention. Admitting early that hitting 20% was ambitious allows you to frame the 5% as a validated, scalable methodology for future $5M projects. This honest yet confident approach shows maturity and realistic planning, which can be just as compelling to top-tier funders as perfect data.",
